:name: EX-B01 - EPS kill switch
:description: COMM, OBC and EPS on a CAN hub, plus a host-driven attacker with no privileges

# Execution profile (design 4.3; rules G1/G2 of section 9.2). Renode's Monitor has no conditionals,
# so the profile is a file the harness swaps by overriding $profile - the same mechanism $injector
# uses, and for the same reason: a relative include inside an included file resolves against
# Renode's own working directory, not this file. Measured: `include @sub/inner.resc` from a script
# elsewhere reports "File does not exist: sub/inner.resc".
#
# This include is FIRST on purpose. A failing command aborts the rest of a .resc file (measured:
# the line after a bad include never runs), so a profile that cannot be found takes the machines
# down with it and the failure is loud. Last, it would have been silent in the worst possible way:
# the scenario would build every node and run with NO quantum set, falling back to Renode's 100 us
# default, which changes firmware timing without any error.
#
# Emulation-scope settings before any machine exists are fine - measured.
#
# The default below only serves someone running this by hand from a clone in $HOME; every harness
# passes an absolute path via src/cuberange/renode/profile.py.
$profile?=@~/space-cs-sim/scripts/profiles/interactive.resc
include $profile

$comm?=@/tmp/cuberange/build-comm/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$obc?=@/tmp/cuberange/build-obc/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$eps?=@/tmp/cuberange/build-eps-vuln/zephyr/zephyr.elf
$commuart?=@/tmp/cuberange/comm.uart
$obcuart?=@/tmp/cuberange/obc.uart
$epsuart?=@/tmp/cuberange/eps.uart
$linkport?=3777
$injport?=3779
# Renode's Monitor cannot concatenate a variable with a literal, so the injector's path is its
# own variable rather than being built from a repo root. The test harness overrides it; the
# default here only serves someone running the scenario by hand from a clone in $HOME.
$injector?=@~/space-cs-sim/attacker/TcpCanInjector.cs

emulation CreateCANHub "canHub"

mach create "COMM"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub
sysbus LoadELF $comm
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $commuart true
emulation CreateServerSocketTerminal $linkport "spacelink" false
connector Connect sysbus.usart2 spacelink
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

mach create "OBC"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub
sysbus LoadELF $obc
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $obcuart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

mach create "EPS"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/nucleo_h753zi.repl
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 canHub
sysbus LoadELF $eps
sysbus.usart3 CreateFileBackend $epsuart true
logLevel 3 sysbus
logLevel 3 rcc
logLevel 3 fdcan1

# The attacker: a bare machine with no platform, no ELF and no CPU. It exists only so the CAN hub
# can resolve GetName()/GetMachine() on the injector - an ICAN attached to a hub must be a
# registered machine peripheral, or the exception poisons the hub for every node on it.
mach create "attacker"
include $injector
machine CreateTcpCanInjector "inj" $injport
connector Connect inj canHub
